> Retain the original thirty-item generator

The original thirty sizes come from a32-bit wrapping linear congruential stream
starting at12345 and the mapping0.15+(state modulo1000)/1000 times0.7. This
generator now lives in the library. The figure shows actual rounded loads after
native exact admission, alongside the capacity-one reference. The table
preserves every original item identity in its assigned bin.

The exact volume lower bound and actual bin count are reported separately.
Equality would certify optimality; a gap alone does not prove either that the
heuristic is suboptimal or that the lower bound is attainable. No real dataset
is forced into this synthetic packing example.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nesting_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nesting.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto sizes = dm::algorithms::nesting_demo_sizes();
    auto a = dm::algorithms::nesting_analyze(sizes, 1);
    std::vector<double> x;
    std::print("Actual items: {}. Bins: {}. Exact volume lower bound: {}. Feasible certificate: {}.\n\n| " "bin | rounded exact load | original item IDs |\n| ---: | ---: | --- |\n",
               sizes.size(), a.result.bins, a.volume_lower_bound,
               dm::algorithms::nesting_feasible(sizes, 1, a.result.assignment));
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.result.loads.size(); ++i) {
        x.push_back(i);
        std::print("| {} | {} |", i, a.result.loads[i]);
        for (auto id : a.result.assignment[i])
            std::print(" {}", id);
        std::print(" |\n");
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.bars(x, a.result.loads, "actual rounded loads", {22, 163, 74}, .7).abline_h(1, {220, 38, 38}, 1).legend({"rounded exact loads", "capacity1"}, {{22, 163, 74}, {220, 38, 38}}).title("Original thirty items: native first-fit-decreasing loads").x_label("actual bin index").y_label("load, capacity1").save_svg("build/nesting_original.svg");
}
```
