> A complete optimality counterexample

For sizes0.4,0.4,0.3,0.3,0.3,0.3, first-fit-decreasing uses three bins: the
two0.4 items together, three0.3 items together, then the last0.3 alone. Yet two
bins each containing0.4+0.3+0.3 are feasible. The native certificate checker
verifies the explicit original-ID assignment, while the exact total volume is
two and its lower bound is two. Therefore the optimum is exactly two and this
heuristic result is strictly suboptimal.

The witness is supplied openly; no hidden exhaustive solver or report-side
packing algorithm generates it. The example explains why descending order and
first fit are a heuristic, even with exact arithmetic. A general approximation
theorem requires a separate proof; this finite example establishes only its
stated optimum and failure of exact optimality.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nesting_counterexample.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nesting.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> s{.4, .4, .3, .3, .3, .3};
    std::vector<std::vector<int>> witness{{0, 2, 3}, {1, 4, 5}};
    auto a = dm::algorithms::nesting_analyze(s, 1);
    bool feasible = dm::algorithms::nesting_feasible(s, 1, witness);
    std::print("| native FFD bins | supplied witness bins | native witness feasible | exact volume lower " "bound |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               a.result.bins, witness.size(), feasible, a.volume_lower_bound);
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(a.result.bins),
                                      double(witness.size()),
                                      double(a.volume_lower_bound)},
                                     {"FFD", "feasible witness", "volume bound"},
                                     "bin count");
    p.title("Six items: greedy 3, certified optimum 2").x_label(
        "packing or lower bound").y_label("bins").save_svg(
        "build/nesting_counterexample.svg");
}
```
